  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The hateful text is mapped onto the Black man with a joyful expression.",
  "description": "The text 'we can kill as many as we want and your stupid government keeps bringing us in' is overlaid on the image of a Black man smiling. The text explicitly targets Muslim communities (implied by the head covering) and Black people (the subject's race), invoking Islamophobia and anti-Black racism. The visual of the smiling man is juxtaposed with the violent message, creating an analogical mapping where the man is implicitly represented as the 'we' in the text — the group being blamed for violence and immigration. This mapping is used to dehumanize and incite fear toward these groups by associating them with the hateful claims.",
